{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "GEN",
  "chapter": 4,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "GEN.4.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.4.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Adam knew Eve his wife; and she conceived, and bore Cain, and said, I have gotten a man from the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.4.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.4.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And she again bore his brother Abel. And Abel was a keeper of sheep, but Cain was a tiller of the ground.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.4.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.4.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And in process of time it came to pass, that Cain brought of the fruit of the ground an offering to the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.4.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.4.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Abel, he also brought of the firstlings of his flock, and of the fat thereof. And the LORD had respect to Abel, and to his offering:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.4.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.4.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But to Cain and to his offering he had not respect. And Cain was very wroth, and his countenance fell.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.4.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.4.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD said to Cain, Why art thou wroth? and why is thy countenance fallen?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.4.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.4.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If thou doest well, shalt thou not be accepted? and if thou doest not well, sin lieth at the door. And to thee ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his desire, and thou shalt rule over him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.4.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.4.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Cain talked with Abel his brother: and it came to pass when they were in the field, that Cain rose up against Abel his brother, and slew him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.4.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.4.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD said to Cain, Where ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Abel thy brother? And he said, I know not: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I my brother's keeper?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.4.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.4.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said, What hast thou done? the voice of thy brother's blood crieth to me from the ground.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.4.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.4.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And now ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou cursed from the earth, which hath opened her mouth to receive thy brother's blood from thy hand;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.4.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.4.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When thou tillest the ground, it shall not henceforth yield to thee its strength: A fugitive and a vagabond shalt thou be in the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.4.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.4.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Cain said to the LORD, My punishment ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " greater than I can bear.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.4.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.4.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, thou hast driven me this day from the face of the earth; and from thy face shall I be hid; and I shall be a fugitive and a vagabond in the earth; and it will come to pass, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " every one that findeth me will slay me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.4.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.4.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD said to him, Therefore whoever slayeth Cain, vengeance shall be taken on him seven-fold. And the lord set a mark upon Cain, lest any finding him should kill him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.4.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.4.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Cain went out from the presence of the LORD, and dwelt in the land of Nod, on the east of Eden.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.4.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.4.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Cain knew his wife, and she conceived, and bore Enoch: and he built a city, and called the name of the city, after the name of his son Enoch.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.4.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.4.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And to Enoch was born Irad: and Irad begat Mehujael: and Mehujael begat Methusael: and Methusael begat Lamech.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.4.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.4.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Lamech took to him two wives: the name of the one ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Adah, and the name of the other Zillah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.4.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.4.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Adah bore Jabal: he was the father of such as dwell in tents, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of such as have",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " cattle.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.4.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.4.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And his brother's name ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Jubal: he was the father of all such as handle the harp and organ.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.4.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.4.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Zillah, she also bore Tubalcain, an instructor of every artificer in brass and iron: and the sister of Tubalcain ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Naamah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.4.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.4.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Lamech said to his wives, Adah and Zillah, Hear my voice, ye wives of Lamech, hearken to my speech: for I have slain a man to my wounding, and a young man to my hurt.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.4.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.4.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If Cain shall be avenged seven-fold, truly Lamech seventy and seven-fold.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.4.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.4.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Adam knew his wife again, and she bore a son, and called his name Seth: For God, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "said she",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", hath appointed me another seed instead of Abel, whom Cain slew.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.4.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.4.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And to Seth, to him also there was born a son; and he called his name Enos: then began men to call upon the name of the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
